With all of these upgrades, the base {{Color|green|10%}} candy chance increases to a {{Green|84%}} chance, or a {{Green|114%}} chance with {{NPCSprite|Foxy}}'s perk. This chance is not increased by {{stat|Magic Find}}.

=== Mob Drops ===
{{Drop Sources}}
Helping kill a {{MobSprite|Headless Horseman}} can also grant '''Green Candy'''. Additionally, {{MobSprite|Bat Piñata}}s will drop '''Green Candy''' when flying around, which can be found randomly during the [[Spooky Festival]] or spawned from a {{Item|Bat Firework}}.

=== Trick or Treat Chests ===
Opening a [[Trick or Treat Chest]] has a {{Green|26.04%}} chance to grant 4-8 '''Green Candy'''.

=== Party Chests ===
Opening a [[Party Chest]] has a {{Green|25.88%}} chance to grant 6-12 '''Green Candy'''.

=== Great Spook Tree ===
A {{Item|Great Spook Tree}} can be placed on the player's {{Zone|Private Island}} to occasionally generate '''Green Candy'''.

=== Garden Visitors ===
Accepting the {{NPCSprite|Fear Mongerer}}'s [[Garden Visitor]] request will grant a '''Green Candy''' or {{Item|Purple Candy}}.

== Usage ==
'''Green Candy''' can be sold on the [[Bazaar]] for varying amounts of coins or traded to the {{NPCSprite|Fear Mongerer}} during the [[Spooky Festival]] for items.

Green candy awards the player +1 point. This is only the case for candies dropped directly from killing mobs or by collecting candies from Bats (excluding players' Bat Fireworks).

